<title>UK: UK's Labour to set inflation target pre-election.</title>
<headline>UK's Labour to set inflation target pre-election.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gordon Brown, finance spokesman for Britain's opposition Labour Party, said on Thursday he would set an inflation target before the general election, in the Party's manifesto if not before.</p>
<p>&quot;We will have a strict inflation target and we will set it at the appropriate time. People have a right to know where we stand on that issue and they will know in our manifesto or before,&quot; he told Reuters Financial Television.  </p>
<p>Underlying inflation is 2.8 percent, a little way above the government's target of 2.5 percent over the medium term.</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett +44 171 542 7715</p>
